format: equavela-worksheet/3
page:
  size: A4
  margins: {top: 54, right: 54, bottom: 54, left: 54}
settings:
  format.precision: 12
regions:
  - id: title
    page: 1
    at: [54, 54]
    text:
      width: full
      text: |
        {style=title}Newton's method

        Newton's method finds a root of a function by following its tangent line down to the axis, again and again. Written as a small program, it shows its famous property: near the root, the number of correct digits doubles at every step.
  - id: h1
    page: 1
    at: [54, 160]
    text: "{style=heading1}The equation"
  - id: t1
    page: 1
    at: [54, 186]
    text:
      width: full
      text: The cubic below is the example Newton himself used. Its derivative is found symbolically, so the iteration needs nothing but the function.
  - id: f
    page: 1
    at: [54, 218]
    math: "f(x) := x^3 − 2·x − 5"
  - id: df
    page: 1
    at: [250, 218]
    math: "df(x) := ⅆ[x] f(x) → "
  - id: h2
    page: 1
    at: [54, 256]
    text: "{style=heading1}The iteration as a program"
  - id: t2
    page: 1
    at: [54, 282]
    text:
      width: full
      text: Each step replaces the estimate $x$ with $x − f(x)/df(x)$. The program collects every estimate in a vector, starting from a rough guess.
  - id: newton
    page: 1
    at: [54, 316]
    math: |
      Newton(x_0, n) := program
        X[0] ← x_0
        for i ∈ 1..n
          X[i] ← X[i − 1] − f(X[i − 1])/df(X[i − 1])
        X
  - id: X
    page: 1
    at: [330, 316]
    math: "X := Newton(3, 6)"
  - id: Xv
    page: 1
    at: [330, 344]
    math: "X = "
  - id: h3
    page: 1
    at: [54, 470]
    text: "{style=heading1}Quadratic convergence"
  - id: t3
    page: 1
    at: [54, 496]
    text:
      width: full
      text: The error of each estimate is measured against the last one. On a logarithmic axis the errors fall along a curve that steepens at every step, and the ratio of each error to the square of the one before settles to a constant, the mark of quadratic convergence.
  - id: r
    page: 1
    at: [54, 548]
    math: "x_r := X[6]"
  - id: k
    page: 1
    at: [160, 548]
    math: "k := 0..4"
  - id: e
    page: 1
    at: [250, 548]
    math: "e[k] := |X[k] − x_r|"
  - id: j
    page: 1
    at: [54, 582]
    math: "j := 0..3"
  - id: ratio
    page: 1
    at: [160, 582]
    math: "c[j] := e[j + 1]/e[j]^2"
  - id: plot
    page: 1
    at: [54, 616]
    plot:
      version: 1
      type: xy
      size: [238, 150]
      axes:
        x: {title: "Step"}
        y: {scale: log10, title: "Error"}
      traces:
        - {id: err, x: "k", y: "e[k]", presentation: line+markers, show_in_legend: false, line: {color: "#00428D"}, marker: {shape: circle, size: 6}}
  - id: c
    page: 1
    at: [330, 616]
    math: "c = "
  - id: t4
    page: 1
    at: [330, 720]
    text:
      width: 211
      text: The constant is $f''(x)/(2·f'(x))$ at the root, about $0.563$ here.
